    story: "<p>Kestrel's new staging environment is yours to build, entirely from the <code>kestrel/infra</code> repository (cloned at <code>~/infra</code>). When you're done:</p><ul>" +
      "<li><b>State</b> in <code>s3://kestrel-tfstate-210987654321/staging/terraform.tfstate</code>, encrypted, with locking (the backend is already in <code>staging/main.tf</code>).</li>" +
      "<li><b>Network</b> from the registry module <code>terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws</code> (version 5): VPC <code>10.50.0.0/16</code>, two public subnets in two AZs.</li>" +
      "<li><b>Two web servers</b> (<code>web-a</code>, <code>web-b</code>, one per subnet) from the latest Ubuntu 24.04, tagged <code>Role=web</code> and <code>Env=staging</code>, IMDSv2 only, encrypted disks; HTTP open to all, SSH only from the office <code>203.0.113.0/24</code>; the ops team's SSH key (yours, <code>~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub</code>) passed in as a variable, not hard-coded.</li>" +
      "<li><b>Checkov</b> reports zero failed checks on <code>staging/</code>: fixed, or suppressed in the resource with a reason.</li>" +
      "<li><b>Changes go through the pipeline</b>: a workflow plans pull requests with the <code>gha-terraform-plan</code> role and applies main with <code>gha-terraform-apply</code> in the <code>production</code> environment (both roles exist). The web servers must be created by the pipeline.</li>" +
      "<li><b>Ansible</b> in <code>ansible/</code> finds the servers with the <code>amazon.aws.aws_ec2</code> inventory (by tag, not by IP), installs nginx with a status page naming the server, turns on ufw (SSH and HTTP only), and writes the notes API key from Vault (<code>secret/notes/api</code>, key <code>key</code>) to <code>/etc/kestrel/api.env</code> readable by root only. A second run changes nothing, and <code>ansible-lint</code> passes.</li></ul>" +
      "<p>No hints on a capstone. A secret the pipeline needs that isn't in the repo goes in a GitHub secret and reaches Terraform as a <code>TF_VAR_</code> environment variable.</p>",
    learn: "<h3>You've got this</h3><p>Everything comes from this module:</p>" +
      '<table class="t"><tr><th>Need</th><th>Lab</th></tr><tr><td>Remote state, locking</td><td>DEV-302</td></tr><tr><td>Variables, registry modules, for_each</td><td>DEV-303</td></tr><tr><td>Network, security groups, hardened EC2</td><td>DEV-304</td></tr><tr><td>Playbooks, idempotency</td><td>DEV-305</td></tr><tr><td>Roles, templates, ufw</td><td>DEV-306</td></tr><tr><td>Vault lookups, root-only secret files</td><td>DEV-307</td></tr><tr><td>Checkov suppressions, ansible-lint</td><td>DEV-308</td></tr><tr><td>OIDC plan/apply pipeline, approvals</td><td>DEV-309</td></tr></table>' +
      "<p>One new piece: Ansible's dynamic inventory for EC2 reads the instances from AWS each run, so new servers are found by their tags:</p>" + code(EC2_INV.replace(/\n$/, "")) + ex("ansible-inventory --graph"),
