    debrief: "<p><b>Module 3 complete.</b> Kestrel's staging environment exists because a repository says so: a network from a pinned registry module, two hardened servers whose every exception is explained in the code, state that's encrypted, locked and shared, a pipeline that plans in the PR and applies only after approval with credentials that can't leak, and Ansible that finds the servers by tag and leaves them identically configured with secrets fetched from Vault. Delete it all and it comes back the same.</p><p>Module 4: running the notes service itself on Kubernetes.</p>",
